# Logitech G502 X PLUS MILLENNIUM FALCON (046d:40b2 through its LIGHTSPEED
# receiver, 046d:c09e cabled) -> uaccess on its own hidraw node through the
# receiver, and on its HID++ interface, 02, on its cable.
#
# Not yet checked on this hardware. It is an edition of the G502 X PLUS with
# ids of its own, so its rules are the X PLUS's hidraw rules in
# 70-g502x.rules, for the same reasons. Through the receiver the mouse's own
# node is matched by its HID device name: a property match would also take
# in the receiver's interfaces, which carry the input of everything paired to
# it. Pair nothing else to this mouse's receiver: going by the kernel's
# hid-logitech-dj.c, a keyboard paired after the mouse could have its
# keystrokes arrive on this node.
#
# The node also carries the keystrokes the mouse sends for a button its
# onboard profile binds to a key, as 70-g502x.rules says of the G502 X PLUS's.
#
# Cabled, a published lsusb of one unit gives three interfaces, 00 a boot
# mouse, 01 a boot keyboard and 02 a vendor collection, the X PLUS's layout,
# where 02 holds HID++ alone; that 02 does here too is assumed. Interface 01
# is not granted.
#
# No event node is granted: in host mode Gearbench reads the buttons it binds
# through HID++ on the hidraw nodes below, and outside host mode none.
KERNEL=="hidraw*", SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", KERNELS=="0003:046D:40B2.*", TAG+="uaccess"
KERNEL=="hidraw*", SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ENV{ID_VENDOR_ID}=="046d", ENV{ID_MODEL_ID}=="c09e", ENV{ID_USB_INTERFACE_NUM}=="02", TAG+="uaccess"
